      ],
      "speaker_hint": "npc",
      "speaker_hint_basis": "character_binding_and_link_parity",
      "EN": "So, you made it to the top and became the Champion of our Arena. Well, that's just a challenge title - nobody can be sure you aren't going to kick the bucket next time. The fights are held more or less regularly - once or twice a day, from 22:00 to 06:00. I'll be posting the arena fight times on the public network anyway so you'll get a heads up if you're interested. As long as you are the Champion, you are welcome to choose any of the announced fights. To put simply, it is up to you to decide who and what to fight with and when. But there are certain limitations about weapons and ammo: it is prohibited to use any kind of explosive ordnance, whether it's grenades or munitions, and especially not heavy weaponry. No grenade launchers, RPGs or those fancy Gauss-rifles, otherwise you're likely to demolish the whole compound and scare off competition, and we don't want that, right? That's it in a nutshell. Now, I have to get the cleaners to mop up the mess you made in there, so you are free to go to the Bar and get totally drunk. But don't be late for the opening! See you!",
      "JA_current": "So, you made it to the top and became the Champion of our Arena. Well, that's just a challenge title - nobody can be sure you aren't going to kick the bucket next time. The fights are held more or less regularly - once or twice a day, from 22:00 to 06:00. I'll be posting the arena fight times on the public network anyway so you'll get a heads up if you're interested. As long as you are the Champion, you are welcome to choose any of the announced fights. To put simply, it is up to you to decide who and what to fight with and when. But there are certain limitations about weapons and ammo: it is prohibited to use any kind of explosive ordnance, whether it's grenades or munitions, and especially not heavy weaponry. No grenade launchers, RPGs or those fancy Gauss-rifles, otherwise you're likely to demolish the whole compound and scare off competition, and we don't want that, right? That's it in a nutshell. Now, I have to get the cleaners to mop up the mess you made in there, so you are free to go to the Bar and get totally drunk. But don't be late for the opening! See you!",
      "string_entry_candidates": [
